  "title": "Dungeons - Project: Gorgon Wiki",
  "main_content": "Dungeons\nFrom Project: Gorgon Wiki\nJump to:\nnavigation\n,\nsearch\nDungeon'\nis a common name for caves, castles, abandoned ruins, and otherworldly realms accessible across\nAlharth\nand beyond. While many\nDungeons\nhave a long-forgotten history, others are homes of sentient Monstrous Races, recently abandoned Council structures, or natural caverns. Adventurers should usually prepare for hostiles, although occasionally paradise and friends can be found. Caves overflowing with Undead, Wolf Dens, and unusually smart insect dwellings are common sights across the continent.\nOnly experienced adventurers should seek out\nDungeons\n, prepared for the\nBosses\n, traps, and deadly puzzles within. Loot and lost abilities can be discovered in dungeons, some dangerous enough that a party of adventurers should brave the mysteries together.\nDungeon Mechanics\nNo Instancing\nDungeons\nin Project: Gorgon are not instanced, and players who enter a dungeon are placed on the same map as all others. In this shared world, loot is usually given to the adventurer who first damages a creature, although\nElite\nMonsters,\nBosses\n, and World Bosses are an exception. If a player opens the loot window for a corpse and closes it without claiming anything, the loot becomes available to everyone else in the area.\n“\nWhen fighting elite and boss monsters, only the first group that attacks it will be able to loot it. (It will become \"locked\" to the first attacker's group, with a little lock icon visible to other groups to let them know.) Each member of the locked group will get their own share of treasure, just as before, but non-group members don't get any loot.\nSolo monsters now become \"open-lootable\" once the original looter closes the corpse. (Meaning that any other player can take leftover loot, autopsy, bury the corpse, etc.)\nClicking on a boss's corpse can now dispel the boss curse even if you don't have loot permissions for the boss\nPreviously when a monster was killed, only the player who had done the highest damage to the monster was recorded as having killed it for certain purposes (such as special behavior badges). Now, anyone who did damage to the creature is counted as a killer\n—\nGame updates/2017-03-25\nDungeon Progression\nDungeon\nLevel\nConnects to\nBosses\nAktaari Cave\n90-95\nErrruka's Cave\nAktaari Princess\nAktaari Queen\nAmaluk Valley Cave\n60 - 70\nGazluk\n,\nFae Realm\nThe Hound of Amaluk Valley\nAnagoge Records Facility\n05 - 10\nAnagoge\n,\nSerbule Hills Spider Cave\nGajus the Big-Headed\nAnimal Nexus\n30 - 35\nEltibule\nThe Magnifier\nThe Maimer\nThe Masher\nThe Mutilator\nBoarded up Basement\n30 - 40\nEltibule\nXegatis\nBorghild\n40 - 45\nSerbule\nForgotten Loading Golem\nKiralem\nVenenae\nBrain Bug Cave\n10 - 15\nSerbule\nCommander Ferrows\nCarpal Tunnels\n25 - 35\nSerbule\nSherzat\nThe Big Slime\nCrystal Cavern\n15 - 20\nSerbule\nMaronesa\nDark Chapel\n40 - 50\nEltibule\nBleddyn\nCrazy Terry\nFear Pump\nFluffy\nHaridius The Exemplary\nKatarina Eltibule\nLord Sedgewick\nMaronesa\nMother Snail\nOld Crusty\nScion of Discord\nSpiderlord\nDungeon Towns\nDungeons by Area\nEltibule Crypt\n20 - 30\nEltibule\nJames Eltibule\nSerisa Eltibule\nElven Judgement\n95\nNightmare Caves\nAmbrosia\nKunax the Dread\n-\nGunn\n-\nSpiderlaird\nErrruka's Cave\n85-90\nPovus\n,\nAktaari Cave\n,\nForthragarian Caves\nExtension:DynamicPageList (DPL), version 2.3.0 : Warning: No results.\nFish Bowl Cavern\n35-40\nSun Vale\nThere are no Boss monsters in the\nFish Bowl Cavern\n.\nForthragarian Caves\n90-95\nErrruka's Cave\n,\nNightmare Caves\nExtension:DynamicPageList (DPL), version 2.3.0 : Warning: No results.\nFungal Fortress\n85\nPovus\nChet Thunder\nEeaeiikik\nEverhorn (mob)\nFear Pump\nFun Guide\nFun Guile\nGue\nGuzyerp\nImarak\nPeacemaster Guztok\nShockybug\nUnfun Guy\nVemuta the Lecturer\nGazluk Keep\n70+\nGazluk\n'Beakhorse'\nArgu the Half-Human\nArkura\nEnvy Pump\nGazluk Clutchmaster\nGut-Ache\nHealing-Suit Tester\